From: Armada FH6 diag <fh6@local>
Subject: [PATCH] tu: report the UMA heap as non-device-local for DXGI memory queries

DXVK sums VK_EXT_memory_budget per segment by VK_MEMORY_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT.
Turnip flags its single system-RAM heap device-local, so the NON_LOCAL segment
reads 0 budget / 0 usage; Forza Horizon 6 (UMA classification) reads that
segment and shows Video Memory 0.00 KB / 0.00 KB, then streams until failure.
Clear the heap flag; memory type property flags are unchanged.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc	2026-10-29 15:16:13.557299900 -0700
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm_msm.cc	2026-10-29 15:16:13.621638500 -0700
@@ -1688,7 +1688,12 @@
 
    device->heap.size = tu_get_system_heap_size(device);
    device->heap.used = 0u;
-   device->heap.flags = VK_MEMORY_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT;
+   /* UMA: leave the heap out of VK_MEMORY_HEAP_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT so DXVK's DXGI
+    * reports budget and usage in DXGI_MEMORY_SEGMENT_GROUP_NON_LOCAL, the segment
+    * a game that classifies this GPU as UMA (Forza Horizon 6) actually reads.
+    * Memory types keep their DEVICE_LOCAL property bits.
+    */
+   device->heap.flags = 0;
 
    instance->knl = &msm_knl_funcs;
 
